[0;1;38;2;95;135;215;49m◆ PRISM TERMINAL[0;2;39;49m › [0;1;39;49mhelp[0m

  This is Prism's terminal site: 434 animated and static terminal facets —
  scenes, spinners, progress meters, charts, text art, TUI controls, diagrams
  and ops views — in 17 galleries, drawn by prism-term 0.2.0, a zero-dependency
  Node engine.

[0;1;38;2;95;135;215;49mBROWSE WITH CURL[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175mcurl -sL prism.jeremyfhall.com/tty          [0;2;39;49mthe terminal site's home[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175mcurl -sL prism.jeremyfhall.com/t/<gallery>  [0;2;39;49mone gallery, by category[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175mcurl -sL prism.jeremyfhall.com/f/<facet>    [0;2;39;49mone facet: still and commands[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175mcurl -sL prism.jeremyfhall.com/t/all        [0;2;39;49mevery facet on one line each[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175mcurl -sL prism.jeremyfhall.com/t/help       [0;2;39;49mthis page[0m

  Pages are stills that fit 80 columns. Long pages: pipe to less -R. Every page
  also comes as:
  [38;2;95;175;175m<page>.txt  [0;2;39;49mplain ASCII, no escape codes — for grep, NO_COLOR, screen readers[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175m<page>.24   [0;2;39;49mtruecolor instead of the default 256 colors[0m
  [0;2;39;49mSearch:   [0;38;2;95;175;175;49mcurl -sL prism.jeremyfhall.com/t/all.txt | grep -i spinner[0m
  [0;2;39;49mPaging:   [0;38;2;95;175;175;49mcurl -sL prism.jeremyfhall.com/t/ops | less -R[0m
  [0;2;39;49mWindows PowerShell 5: type [0;38;2;95;175;175;49mcurl.exe[0;2;39;49m (plain "curl" is an alias there).[0m
  [0;2;39;49mPowerShell and cmd don't continue lines with \: join a command that ends[0m
  [0;2;39;49min \ with the next line (drop the \) before you run it.[0m

[0;1;38;2;95;135;215;49mTHE LIVE PLAYER[0m
  The live player renders facets in real time and detects your terminal
  (truecolor, 256, 16, mono; braille and block glyphs, or plain ASCII). It needs
  Node 18+ and no network after the download.
[38;2;95;175;175m  npx -y --package=https://prism.jeremyfhall.com/dl/prism-term.tgz prism-term[0m
[0;2;39;49m  …then add a command:[0m
    [38;2;95;175;175m(none)            [0;2;39;49mbrowse the catalog: arrows move, / searches, Enter plays[0m
    [38;2;95;175;175mplay <facet>      [0;2;39;49mone facet fullscreen (--size 80x24, --depth 256, --ascii)[0m
    [38;2;95;175;175mlist              [0;2;39;49mevery facet, grouped by gallery[0m
    [38;2;95;175;175msnapshot <facet>  [0;2;39;49mprint one still frame to stdout[0m
[0;2;39;49m  Prefer a permanent install? Run this once, then just type prism-term:[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175mnpm i -g https://prism.jeremyfhall.com/dl/prism-term.tgz[0m

[0;1;38;2;95;135;215;49mGALLERIES[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175mfx         objects    sim        retro      text       loaders[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175mprogress   charts     ai         status     ops        diagrams[0m
  [38;2;95;175;175mcallouts   input      maps       lab        ascii[0m

[0;1;38;2;95;135;215;49mFOR AGENTS AND TOOLS[0m
  Machine-readable: the JSON island <script id="prism-terminal-catalog"> in the
  web catalog, prism.jeremyfhall.com/Prism.html, and the same catalog at
  prism.jeremyfhall.com/terminal/engine/catalog/terminal-catalog.json. Each
  facet record has id, gallery, category, tags, size, glyphs, color depth,
  params, a plain-text preview and its module path; the module's code, and the
  "_" helpers it imports, are in the catalog's top-level "sources".

